**Loan Agreement**

**January 14, 2021**

**WHEREAS**, ABC Bank ("Lender") is a duly organized and existing bank chartered under the laws of the State of Delaware, with its principal place of business at 123 Main Street, Wilmington, Delaware 19801; and

**WHEREAS**, XYZ Corporation ("Parent Company"), a Delaware corporation, having its principal place of business at 456 Park Avenue, New York, New York 10016, is the parent company of DEF Subsidiary Inc. ("Subsidiary"), a Delaware corporation, having its principal place of business at 789 Business Street, San Francisco, California 94101;

**WHEREAS**, Parent Company and Subsidiary have applied to Lender for a loan of USD $5,000,000.00 (the "Loan"); and

**WHEREAS**, Lender has agreed to make the Loan to Parent Company and Subsidiary, subject to the terms and conditions set forth in this Loan Agreement (the "Agreement").

**1. Loan Terms**

1.1 The Loan shall consist of a principal amount of USD $5,000,000.00, payable in ten (10) equal monthly installments commencing on February 14, 2021.

1.2 The Loan shall bear interest at the rate of 5.0% per annum, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year, and shall be payable in arrears.

1.3 The Loan shall be secured by Parent Company's and Subsidiary's respective assets, as further described in the Security Agreement (the "Security Agreement") to be entered into by the parties concurrently with this Agreement.

**2. Interest and Fees**

2.1 In addition to the interest payable on the Loan, Parent Company and Subsidiary shall pay Lender a commitment fee of 0.25% per annum on the outstanding principal amount of the Loan, payable quarterly in arrears.

2.2 Parent Company and Subsidiary shall also pay all fees and expenses incurred by Lender in connection with the Loan, including, without limitation, legal fees, appraisal fees, and filing fees.

**3. Default and Remedies**

3.1 In the event Parent Company or Subsidiary fails to perform any of its obligations under this Agreement, Lender shall have the right to declare the entire outstanding principal amount of the Loan immediately due and payable.

3.2 In the event of a default under this Agreement, Lender shall have the right to exercise all rights and remedies available under applicable law, including, without limitation, the right to foreclose on the Security, to seize and sell Parent Company's and Subsidiary's assets, and to bring suit against Parent Company and Subsidiary for any unpaid amounts.

**4. Representations and Warranties**

Parent Company and Subsidiary represent and warrant to Lender as follows:

4.1 Each of Parent Company and Subsidiary is duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation.

4.2 Each of Parent Company and Subsidiary has full power and authority to execute and deliver this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

**5. Governing Law**

This Agreement shall be governed by, and construed in accordance with, the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict of laws principles.

**6. Counterparts**

This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument.

**7. Entire Agreement**

This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior negotiations, understandings, and agreements between the parties, whether written or oral.

**8. Amendments**

This Agreement may not be amended or modified except by a written instrument executed by all parties hereto.

**In Witness Whereof**, Parent Company, Subsidiary, and Lender have executed this Agreement as of the date first above written.

